    "instructions": "Cupertino components draw iOS-style controls on every platform. Bind a control's current value with {\"@path\": \"/settings/wifi\"} (RFC 6901, leading slash) so user input writes back to the data model; send initial values in updateDataModel. Use CupertinoAlertDialog for a confirm-or-cancel question, opened by its trigger child; tapping the trigger opens the alert and also runs the trigger's own action. Prefer these components when the surface should look native on iOS; mix them with basic components only where no Cupertino counterpart exists. A segmented control draws at most 6 segments; the rest are cut and reported. A slider whose max is not above its min is drawn from 0 to 1.",
